-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source adapted from XLA and JAX
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Besides linking XLA, parts of the plugin's own source are adapted from XLA
(https://github.com/openxla/xla, Copyright The OpenXLA Authors) and from JAX
(https://github.com/jax-ml/jax, Copyright The JAX Authors), both under the
Apache License 2.0, the license of this project (LICENSE):

- metal_pjrt/compiler/metal_compiler.{h,cc} follow XLA's
  xla/service/gpu/intel_gpu_compiler.{h,cc}, and the StreamExecutor classes
  in metal_pjrt/stream_executor/ follow the interfaces and layout of XLA's
  xla/stream_executor/cuda and rocm platforms.
- metal_pjrt/codegen/msl_emitter.cc repeats the pass list of
  AddLoweringPasses in XLA's
  xla/backends/gpu/codegen/emitters/mlir_kernel_emitter.cc, and
  metal_pjrt/kernels/msl_prelude.metal uses the erf approximation of
  xla/codegen/emitters/transforms/expand_float_ops.cc.
- metal_pjrt/xla_tripwire/golden.txt and oneapi_callsites.txt are excerpts
  of XLA's source, kept to detect changes when the XLA pin moves.
- third_party/xla/patches are changes to XLA's own files; the abseil,
  protobuf and gRPC patches in third_party/ are copied from JAX's and
  XLA's third_party/ directories.
- jax_graft/__init__.py follows JAX's jax_plugins/cuda plugin
  module, and jax_graft/_callbacks.py repeats the result checks of
  jax/_src/callback.py.


